# Directories that get a `claude rc` Remote Control session at boot.
#
#   - One directory per line.
#   - Blank lines and #-comments are ignored.
#   - "~" is expanded; relative paths are not allowed.
#   - The session name shown in claude.ai/code is the directory's basename.
#     Duplicate basenames get -2, -3, ... appended.
#
# After editing this file, apply it with:   claude-rc-ctl sync
# (no reboot needed; unchanged entries are left running untouched)
#
# NOTE: a directory must have been trusted once by running `claude` in it
# interactively. `claude-rc-ctl list` shows trust status per entry.

~/repos/my-project
~/docker
